    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Kyle Schwarber** (72.77). **Yordan Alvarez** faces the most favorable matchup of the evening against the 6.12 xERA of Klassen, benefiting from an elite xwOBA profile that maximizes his raw power potential. Meanwhile, **Kyle Schwarber** and **Trea Turner** (72.38) are locked into premium leadoff and two-hole spots respectively against Gibson; while the platoon advantage for these lefties is marginal, their elevated lineup positions provide the optimal runway for run production. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (67.94) remains a strong play, leveraging a significant 16% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Rod\u00f3n to provide reliable value at the corner.\n\nThe decision to start **Caleb Durbin** (67.40) over the rest of the bench was driven largely by our internal mandate to prioritize speed-heavy profiles in a 5x5 Roto format. While **Colt Keith** (45.95) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine, his lower projected efficiency\u2014hampered by the difficult 3.26 xERA of Ashcraft\u2014could not compete with the total output projection of the active roster. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (55.70) remains in the lineup despite a tough platoon disadvantage against the left-handed Hudson; his inclusion is tactical, as his 87% stolen base success rate and the potential for a slow delivery from the mound make him a necessary catalyst for our scarce SB category. We are monitoring the weather for any late-breaking system changes, but as it stands, the lineup is optimized to maximize plate appearances for our high-OBP threats against vulnerable arms like Kelly and Martinez.",
